---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { VALUES, BANDS, slugFor, bandFor, REF_LOW, REF_HIGH, TREAT_HIGH } from '../../data/tsh-levels';

const title = 'TSH Levels by Number: Look Up Your Result';
const description =
  'Find your exact TSH result and what it means. Every level from 0.01 to 100 mIU/L, with the reference range, the treatment threshold and what to test alongside.';

const grouped = BANDS.map((b) => ({
  band: b,
  values: VALUES.filter((v) => bandFor(v).id === b.id),
})).filter((g) => g.values.length > 0);

const canonical = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site).toString();
const schemas = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'MedicalWebPage',
    name: title,
    description,
    about: { '@type': 'MedicalTest', name: 'Thyroid stimulating hormone (TSH) test' },
    mainEntityOfPage: { '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': canonical },
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: new URL('/', Astro.site).toString() },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'TSH levels', item: canonical },
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={`${title} — Bevita`} description={description} schemas={schemas} image="/images/bevita-insulin-resistance-screen.jpg">
  <article class="hub">
    <header class="hub-head">
      <div class="shell">
        <a href="/blog/" class="back">← Bevita blog</a>
        <h1>TSH levels by number</h1>
        <p class="lede">{description}</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="body shell">
      <p>
        A TSH result is easy to look up and hard to interpret, because the same number means
        different things depending on where it falls. The usual adult reference range is roughly
        <strong>{REF_LOW} to {REF_HIGH} mIU/L</strong>, and treatment for an underactive thyroid is
        typically considered above <strong>{TREAT_HIGH} mIU/L</strong> — but the interesting
        territory is everything in between.
      </p>
      <p>
        Pick your value below. Each page covers what that specific level means, what tends to cause
        it, whether treatment is usually indicated, and which tests belong alongside it. If your
        exact number isn't listed, the nearest one will read the same way.
      </p>

      {grouped.map((g) => (
        <section class="group">
          <h2>{g.band.label}</h2>
          <p class="range">
            {g.band.max === Infinity
              ? `Above ${g.band.min} mIU/L`
              : `${g.band.min} – ${g.band.max} mIU/L`}
            {' · '}{g.band.verdict}
          </p>
          <ul class="grid">
            {g.values.map((v) => (
              <li><a href={`/tsh/${slugFor(v)}/`}>TSH {v}</a></li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </section>
      ))}

      <h2>Reading a TSH result properly</h2>
      <p>
        TSH runs opposite to thyroid output: it rises when the thyroid underperforms and falls when
        it overperforms. That's why a high TSH means an <em>underactive</em> thyroid, which catches
        most people out. For the mechanism, start with{' '}
        <a href="/blog/high-tsh-thyroid-explained/">what a high TSH is actually telling you</a>, and
        for the hormones TSH is regulating, see{' '}
        <a href="/blog/free-t3-t4-explained/">free T3 and free T4 explained</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Two caveats apply to every value on this page. Reference ranges differ between laboratories,
        so compare against the range printed on your own report rather than a range from the
        internet. And single readings fluctuate — TSH peaks overnight, shifts with illness, and
        responds slowly to real change, so the trend across several tests carries more information
        than any one result.
      </p>

      <h2>Related guides</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/blog/high-tsh-thyroid-explained/">High TSH: what your thyroid is actually telling you</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/high-tsh-causes/">What causes high TSH</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/high-tsh-symptoms/">High TSH symptoms</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/high-tsh-high-t4/">High TSH with high T4</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/tsh-over-100/">TSH over 100</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/hyperthyroidism-tsh/">Hyperthyroidism and TSH</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/ultrasensitive-tsh/">Ultrasensitive TSH explained</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/thyroid-antibodies-tpo/">Thyroid antibodies (TPO)</a></li>
      </ul>

      <p class="disclaimer">
        This page is for education and isn't medical advice. Discuss your results with a qualified
        clinician.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="cta shell">
      <div class="cta-box">
        <h3>Track your TSH instead of looking it up</h3>
        <p>
          Upload your lab reports to Bevita and it keeps every TSH and free T4 with its date, charts
          the trend, and reads them against the symptoms you log. Free to start.
        </p>
        <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/bevita-blood-test-labs/id6783030563" class="badge">Download on the App Store</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .shell { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
  .hub-head { padding: 120px 0 32px; }
  .back { display: inline-block; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-3); margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .back:hover { color: var(--forest); }
  .lede { font-size: 20px; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 54ch; }
  .body { padding-block: 8px 64px; }
  .body h2 { margin-top: 48px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .body p { margin-bottom: 16px; max-width: 65ch; }
  .body ul { margin-bottom: 16px; padding-left: 24px; }
  .body li { margin-bottom: 8px; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 17px; }
  .body a { color: var(--forest); font-weight: 500; }
  .body a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .group { margin-top: 40px; }
  .group h2 { margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .range { font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-3); margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .grid { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .grid li { margin: 0; }
  .grid a {
    display: inline-block; padding: 8px 14px; border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: 15px;
  }
  .grid a:hover { border-color: var(--forest); text-decoration: none; }
  .disclaimer { font-style: italic; color: var(--ink-3); font-size: 15px; margin-top: 32px; }
  .cta { padding-block: 0 96px; }
  .cta-box {
    background: var(--tinted); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 32px; text-align: center;
  }
  .cta-box h3 { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .cta-box p { margin: 0 auto 20px; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 16px; max-width: 44ch; }
  .badge {
    display: inline-block; padding: 10px 20px; border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--ink); color: var(--on-brand); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 500;
  }
</style>
